<Project>

  <!--
    Vixen — test-only source shared across test assemblies, linked rather than referenced.

    Imported by every test project that asserts on allocation. Adds Measured, the guarded
    replacement for a bare `GC.GetAllocatedBytesForCurrentThread()` subtraction; the file itself
    says why the subtraction is not enough.

    LINKED, NOT A PROJECT, for three reasons:

      1. Directory.Build.props gives every non-test project under Core/ the runtime profile —
         packable, AOT-compatible, trimmable, documentation file required. All four are wrong for
         test-only code, so a Core/Vixen.Testing library would need either a fourth profile or a
         name that lies about what it is.
      2. A referenced assembly would have to make Measured public and would flow xunit into every
         consumer transitively. A linked file keeps it internal, per assembly, and adds nothing to
         any test output.
      3. The repository already links source across project boundaries where an assembly boundary
         would be the wrong shape — see Vixen.Input.Generators and Vixen.Ui.Markup.Generators.

    Top level rather than under Core/ because docs/plan/02 § "Core/" states that every folder there
    is one class library plus its sibling test project, and this is neither. It is also where the
    shared test infrastructure of docs/plan/12 § "Test infrastructure worth building early" belongs
    when it is written — RecordingBackend and TestApp are here now, each beside its own props file;
    GoldenFile and FixtureProject are still owed, and are tracked as #336.

    Consumers need a `using Vixen.Testing;` and a PackageReference to xunit.v3, which every test
    project in the tree already has.
  -->

  <ItemGroup>
    <Compile Include="$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)Measured.cs" Link="Testing\Measured.cs" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
